{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me","id":1005544,"title":"[Discipline] Celerity Bugs Me","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-19T19:28:44-08:00","id":1005544,"title":"[Discipline] Celerity Bugs Me","content":"It's mostly that it doesn't even really fit with the other two Physicals - plus, the extra resource you have to track offends my sense of aesthetics. Unt so:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>C</b>elerity</span><br /> <i>Insert descriptive text from B&amp;S here</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> None or One Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> None (For persistent effects) or Reflexive (For active effects)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent (For persistent effects) or Instant (For active effects)<br /> <br /> Like other physical Disciplines, Celerity has two kinds of effects: persistent and active. Persistent effects are always on, and have no cost. Active effects are Reflexive, and cost one Vitae per effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent:</b> Add the Vampire's dots in Celerity to their Dexterity; this may raise a character's Dexterity above the limit imposed by their Blood Potency. Additionally, add the Vampire's dots in Celerity to their Speed.<br /> <br /> <b>Active:</b> By spending Vitae, the Kindred may bring the frightful swiftness of their Beast to the fore, striking their victims before they even realize it. For every Vitae spent, chose one effect from the following list. A vampire may spend additional Vitae to invoke multiple effects simultaneously, but no effect of Celerity may be used more than once per turn.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Add thrice your dots in Celerity to your Speed this turn.<br /> \u2022 Attacks made against you this turn take a penalty equal to your dots in Celerity.<br /> \u2022 Immediately take the Break Free or Take Cover moves without rolling. <hr /><br /> It's rather different from the canon Celerity, I know - it's a bit more focused on being inhumanly agile and fast rather than being superhumanly fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 11-19-2016, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T20:12:09-08:00","id":1005555,"title":"","content":"There was some major reasoning behind it not adding to Dexterity, I think something akin to it amounting to a god stat (especially in regard to fire arms + defense at times) which is why it added to defense directly. You've greatly weakened celerity in general with your active effects so I guess that could offset it, but it completely kills the vampire-superspeed aesthetic (Your adding not multiplying)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T20:45:29-08:00","id":1005569,"title":"","content":"The god-stat thing - think of it this way:<br /> <br /> <b>Celerity</b> adds to your attack pool for Athletics/Firearms attacks.<br /> <b>Vigor</b> adds to your attack pool for Brawl/Weaponry attacks, and you can spend Vitae to add [Vigor] successes to successful Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry attacks this turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Celerity</b> adds to Defense (up to a point), and you can spend Vitae to subtract [Celerity] dice from all attacks made against you this turn.<br /> <b>Resilience</b> adds to your HLs and downgrades [Resilience] levels of Aggravated damage, and you can spend Vitae to subtract [Resilience] <i>successes</i> from a single attack, or just subtract damage from a non-attack source.<br /> <br /> Firearms are actually kind of terrible as far as Kindred are concerned - they only take Bashing from them. It's a lot more efficient, violence-wise, to get all up in your opponent's grill with an axe or grapple (not in the <i>least</i> because Vigor straight-up adds to the damage). So in the specific context of Vampire, &quot;I is good at shotting people&quot; is less of a concern. As for Defense, the canon way is straight-up better at it than the passive benefit.<br /> <hr /><br /> I think I'll throw in +Celerity to Speed as part of the Persistent benefit, and up the active ability to 3x. That way, you're looking at a potential +5 to Speed per dot - your Vigor 5/Celerity 5 Daeva would potentially have 30 Speed over the competition, which is nothing to sneeze at.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T21:03:03-08:00","id":1005576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005569#post1005569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firearms are actually kind of terrible as far as Kindred are concerned - they only take Bashing from them. It's a lot more efficient, violence-wise, to get all up in your opponent's grill with an axe or grapple (not in the <i>least</i> because Vigor straight-up adds to the damage).</div> </div> </div> </div>They take only Bashing damage from <i>all</i> weapons, so being able to add damage with Vigor is the only reason an axe would be more efficient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T21:50:09-08:00","id":1005595,"title":"","content":"Firearms also ignore defense in most cases (save for a Devotion, and you get your Celerity dots as defense), and firearms also give you a range advantage. Guns are still better than melee against Kindred, barring specialization (particularly Claws of the Unholy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T22:31:31-08:00","id":1005604,"title":"","content":"Staking via crossbow would be much easier.<br /> <br /> I figured the thing is that Dexterity is not something you can just 'power up,' and it's not just agility, it's hand-eye coordination and balance. If Celerity added to it passively it would be like turning your fingers into tentacles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T02:44:19-08:00","id":1005643,"title":"","content":"I think this version of celerity is too much underpowered (for active effects) in front of Vigor and Resilence:<br /> - With Vigor you multiply the range of jump why celerity should just add to your speed (and it's passive for vigor)? <br /> - resilence soak resilence+1 damage while celerity simply subtract to the attacker pool.<br /> Honestly I'd never take this version of celerity. <br /> Why a vampire can't be superhumanly fast if she can jump 40-50 yards and go throught a fire without being damaged at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T04:09:27-08:00","id":1005654,"title":"","content":"I kinda think the Passive Power of Celerity isn't up to snuff.<br /> <br /> Vigor/Resilience get Strength/Stamina increases.<br /> Celerity gets Defense instead of Dexterity. I'm kinda fine with this, because giving Dex might not improve Defense, and Celerity is only about the speed part of Dexterity anyway.<br /> <br /> However Vigor also get extra attack dice in Melee, through the Strength. And jumping ability.<br /> Resilience get an extra health level. And the ability to downgrade non-sun aggravated damage.<br /> Celerity gets nothing else.<br /> <br /> The passive parts just don't seem very balanced.<br /> <br /> Passively I think they should still be faster. And not just in Defense. But in Attack too. Giving them Celerity bonus to their initiative would seem right to me. A 1 initiative per Celerity level (maybe even 2, or C+1). How do I answer a Daeva who says &quot;if I'm faster why don't I attack faster?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm honestly tempted to house rule it. And would but for the fact that I have literally, and deliberately, avoided doing any house rules.<br /> <br /> I wonder why the design choice was made to give them the short end of passive powers? Assuming they'd even accept they may have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","user":"FutureBondVillain","date":". 11-20-2016, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T05:15:00-08:00","id":1005667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005654#post1005654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do I answer a Daeva who says &quot;if I'm faster why don't I attack faster?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, partly because in a one-on-one fight the most effective use of celerity involves <i>not</i> going first. If you wait until your opponent takes their action and spend a vitae to interrupt it, you can basically lock them down for [celerity] turns, which at high levels could easily win you the fight.<br /> <br /> Also they appear to have traded a passive bonus to initiative for an active &quot;just go first&quot;. Presumably for when you run out of uses for the above trick and the guy's still standing. Let's you get in one final blow before they can act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T05:20:05-08:00","id":1005670,"title":"","content":"Basic Celerity is why Brawl is the best attack skill. If you can beat your opponent in a grapple, you use a single dot of Celerity to surprise the target (negating the bonus) or reflexively attack them. Then they can't autododge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T06:33:05-08:00","id":1005684,"title":"","content":"I think you're overlooking a major power of Celerity in that active currently gives you an extra action per use of the interrupt feature(up to Celerity dots per scene). It says you may only make one instant action with it, but it says nothing about losing your normal action on your own turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T06:37:55-08:00","id":1005687,"title":"","content":"You only get one instant action in a turn, even with Celerity. This was a deliberate departure from the ridiculously broken Celerity of oWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T06:43:36-08:00","id":1005690,"title":"","content":"Oh. Page reference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T06:51:06-08:00","id":1005693,"title":"","content":"<i>The very line you quoted. </i>That's what it meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T07:20:05-08:00","id":1005697,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;She cannot use Celerity to make two attacks, or an attack followed by another instant action.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I'm not so sure that's what it means. It says nothing about a turn, it just says this power itself can't give two actions, just one.<br /> The next sentence goes on to specifically state the power's per turn limits. &quot;...<i>you cannot move further in a single turn than her Speed would allow</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, why limit to X uses per scene if that's the case? The Masquerade one was broken because you could spam it ad infitum. It's not spammably broken in any way if you can only use it to replace your current action with a half-action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T07:44:57-08:00","id":1005704,"title":"","content":"Someone attempts to melee attack you; you interrupt to move your Speed away from them. Their attack fails because you are now out of range. Moving isn't an instant action, so you still have one when your turn comes around. You shoot them in the face with a shotgun. This is what Celerity's interrupt allows you to do. It is incredibly powerful. But you don't get a second instant action in a turn, and you can't move more than your normal per-turn limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T08:02:00-08:00","id":1005707,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I think I'll keep my interpretation for my own games though because an extra attack up to Celerity times per scene and for a Vitae each is no more broken than that scenario IMO. Plus it makes no sense that one would be so fast and with such twitchy reflexes that they can make extreme rapid and far reaching motions in any direction at any time... <i>except</i> towards a hostile party.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it's vaguely worded for ST's to make what they will of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T08:14:48-08:00","id":1005712,"title":"","content":"The key word here is <i>likewise. </i>The full quote goes<i>, &quot;</i>She cannot use Celerity to make two attacks, or an attack followed by another instant action. <b>Likewise</b> she cannot move further in a single turn than her Speed would allow.&quot;<br /> <br /> That implies that the first sentence refers to the turn as a whole, not simply the celerity actions. You're <i>already </i>not allowed to make multiple interruptions because you can only use each active power once per turn anyway, so I don't really see any way of taking two actions in a turn <i>except </i>to do what you're arguing should be allowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-20-2016, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T08:53:21-08:00","id":1005720,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why you're saying &quot;except towards a hostile party.&quot; It doesn't let you pick two locks in a turn or use two Instant-action Disciplines in a turn, either. You get one Instant action per turn. Attacking twice in a turn is functionally almost the same as having another combatant on your side. The only real difference is that you're health pool isn't also doubled. Action economy is a huge balancing factor in RPGs. If a game allows multiple actions per round, it becomes a must-have for everyone who wants to be passable at combat. That's why it's so rare/nonexistant in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T10:39:58-08:00","id":1005756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005667#post1005667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, partly because in a one-on-one fight the most effective use of celerity involves <i>not</i> going first.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're explaing the best use of Celerity. That doesn't explain why they're not faster (in Attack).<br /> <br /> Passively: The Vigors are stronger. The Resiliencers are more durable. The Celerities are only faster in Defense. The others get 3 passive powers. The Celerity dudes get 1. <br /> <br /> Really though, why should it make you faster in Defense, but not faster to Attack? (Passively)<br /> <br /> It's not like say C (or C+1) bonus to Initiative would even be THAT powerful.<br /> <br /> If the Developers were weakening its Passive Power deliberately to balance its Active power, I could understand that. I don't feel that is the case though. Celerities Active use is limited, whereas the other two aren't. I feel that was the balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T10:58:27-08:00","id":1005763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005756#post1005756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're explaing the best use of Celerity. That doesn't explain why they're not faster (in Attack).</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>Are</i> faster in attack, insofar as the system models attack speed - if they want to go first, they can always go first. Only another supernatural speed ability can prevent them from doing so, and only with a successful Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005756#post1005756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Passively: The Vigors are stronger. The Resiliencers are more durable. The Celerities are only faster in Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, CofD's combat system doesn't really model attack speed very well. No matter how fast you are, it's still a turn-based system and you can only attack once per turn. That means the only way you can really represent the speed of an attack is by allowing it to happen first. Which Celerity does. Even better, it actually allows you to interrupt another character's action, partially bypassing the normal rules of the turn-based system (without actually breaking the action economy).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005756#post1005756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The others get 3 passive powers. The Celerity dudes get 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how you're arriving at this conclusion. Vigor only raises Strength passively and Resilience only raises Stamina passively. Granted, more derived traits key off of Strength and Stamina than off of Defense, but Celerity also adds to your Dodge pool after doubling Defense, and it applies against Firearms, so you could call that 3 things too if you wanted to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005756#post1005756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really though, why should it make you faster in Defense, but not faster to Attack? (Passively)</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it wouldn't really be useful to do so. Celerity allows you to bypass the initiative system actively, so Passive Initiative boosting would be redundant. Besides, it actually hampers the interrupt ability, which is more effective if your &quot;natural&quot; Initiative is lower so you can see what your opponent is going to do before interrupting it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005756#post1005756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like say C (or C+1) bonus to Initiative would even be THAT powerful.<br /> <br /> If the Developers were weakening its Passive Power deliberately to balance its Active power, I could understand that. I don't feel that is the case though. Celerities Active use is limited, whereas the other two aren't. I feel that was the balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a balance thing, I think it's just a matter of a Passive Initiative boost not actually helping Celerity users most of the time, and even hindering them at some times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:03:31-08:00","id":1005765,"title":"","content":"Well, celerity has <i>always </i>been the odd one out of the physical disciplines. Back in 1e vigor and resilience cost 1 vitae to activate what are now their passive effects for a scene, while celerity only got it's speed boost for a turn. Obviously, they couldn't just have celerity users speedblitzing all the time for free, so when they shifted to 2e they had to do celerity a bit differently.<br /> <br /> Oh, also I'm not sure an initiative boost would be <i>that</i> detrimental to interrupting an action - it seems silly to say that a character can't simply delay their turn until the person they want to interrupt goes. so at worst the bonus would be irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-20-2016, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:17:41-08:00","id":1005767,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin, most of your post is using Active powers to support the Passive powers weakness.<br /> <br /> My whole post, and the other one, is making the case that the *Passive powers* don't seem to balance. So bringing Active powers into that discussion isn't the way to address it.<br /> <br /> I'm not bringing Vigor/Resilience Active powers into the argument.<br /> <br /> The Active use is number limited in addition to all that. Tell me how great your Celerity two Active power is, and you don't need an Initiative boost, after you've interrupted twice.<br /> <br /> If the Developers goal was that the Active powers of Celerity overcome some of the weaknesses of the Passive powers then I'd see the argument. I might or might not agree with it. But, either way, it doesn't aeem to be the case.<br /> <br /> You're ignoring the other extra Passive powers of V/R, I pointed out in my first post. And not the ones that key off Strength/Stamina. Extra whole new powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:29:16-08:00","id":1005771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005767#post1005767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell me how great your Celerity two Active power is, and you don't need an Initiative boost, after you've interrupted twice.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, generally, it's because the person you were fighting isn't a threat any more. <br /> <br /> It's limited because it's <i>really powerful. </i>And also not the actual iconic celerity power, which is the third one. Which is <i>not</i> limited per scene, and is in fact <i>also</i> really powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:35:03-08:00","id":1005773,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you're trying to say here, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12158\" data-vbnamecard=\"12158\">FutureBondVillain</a> . You're all over the place and even contradicting yourself (you say bringing Active powers in is wrong, just before you bring Active powers into the discussion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:39:29-08:00","id":1005778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005773#post1005773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you're trying to say here, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12158\" data-vbnamecard=\"12158\">FutureBondVillain</a> . You're all over the place and even contradicting yourself (you say bringing Active powers in is wrong, just before you bring Active powers into the discussion).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kinda in response to the people who seem unable to argue Celerities case with bringing them into the argument.<br /> <br /> I think the Passive powers should be argued on there own. But I'm seeing others not happy to do that. Repeatedly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","user":"FutureBondVillain","date":". 11-20-2016, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:53:07-08:00","id":1005781,"title":"","content":"I keep bringing up active powers because your suggestion for how to improve Celerity's passive power is by adding it to Initiative. But Celerity's active power already circumvents the initiative. I'm not saying, &quot;Celerity has active initiative jumping, therefore it's Passive isn't underpowered,&quot; I'm saying, &quot;Celerity has active initiative jumping, therefore Passive Initiative bonus wouldn't improve Celerity's Passive power, and would in fact weaken the Discipline as a whole.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't really agree that Celerity's Passive is underpowered, but you do and that's enough to justify house ruling it in your games. I'm just telling you your proposed house rule doesn't seem like it will actually help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:12:35-08:00","id":1005793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005778#post1005778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Passive powers should be argued on there own. But I'm seeing others not happy to do that. Repeatedly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is pretty much my how I feel. Celerity is a very active power, so ignoring it's active effects is basically ignoring celerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T08:16:04-08:00","id":1006198,"title":"","content":"I thought Celerity was one of the best changes 2E made. It took one of the worst disciplines and made it super awesome.<br /> <br /> I don't agree that passive Celerity is underpowered. At level 1 or 2, maybe, but so is Vigor. Also, speaking of passive power, they don't have 2 or 3 aspects. Vigor only boosts strength. Then, in turn, strength boosts attack, but that's not a different power, it's the same thing. Same with Resilience boosting Stamina and HP, HP is calculated with stamina, so yeah, duh. What Resilience does, though, is downgrade (non-sun) aggravated, which is very good, but aggravated doesn't really come up that often that it's a game changer.<br /> <br /> Passive Celerity adds to defence. That is a direct counter to vigor, basically. One character with x in Vigor attacking a character with x in Celerity means both cancel each other and the attack dice pool is the same as if nobody had disciplines. Aside from that vigor does give a slight extra edge in making the user able to use bigger weapons which will hurt more, but you're gonna need obfuscate if you want to carry a buster sword around. On the other hand, and that is important, Celerity provides defence against firearms. Nobody gets that except broken as shit gaurou werewolves.<br /> <br /> Now, sure, we're talking about &quot;only&quot; a potential 5 bonus in defence, but unless you're only fighting very powerful supernaturals, A boost of 3 to 5 in defence potentially makes you unhittable by anyone. The average Dexerity/Wits score is 2, and any decent PC who wants to fight will have at least 1 in athletics. Add celerity 3 to it and you get 6 defence. According to some supplement which I'm not sure about (maybe armory), competent but common fighters or firerarms users will tend to get a score of 2 in their skill. I think that was the score for your average soldier or something. It represents limited but professional training, so you'll have to piss off some really nasty people to have more dangerous guys than that thrown at your in large numbers. So let's say we have a sword fighter with Strength 3 and 2 in weaponry for an attack pool of 5 and a shooter with Dex 3 and firearm 2 :<br /> <br /> In normal attacks, the fighter will have to throw a chance die to have a chance to hit your vampire. The shooter will have only 2 dice, which isn't so great (and worsened as soon as the vampire gets in range or takes some form of cover). The fighter has to use willpower to only get 2 attack dice, and the shooter, with willpower will get back what should have been his original 5 dice pool. That is a big deal. Celerity makes you untouchable against mooks.<br /> <br /> You have to take into account the way defence is calculated now. The fact athletics (or brawl/weaponry) is added means that, since you still take the lower od dex/wits, your average defense score will only be marginally inferior to your average attack pool. The same way vigor breaks that balance and give its user a big advantage, so does celerity. The difference is that, against mooks, vigor user can still get hit regularly if they don't have the initiative and one-shot their opponent, celerity, while not making the fight faster, means you can more easily get out of it unharmed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, the most interesting part of new celerity is the new active power of interruption, which allows for tactical thinking and can ruin an opponent's day without the multiple attack madness of the CWoD celerity or the crazy styles of 1E (looking at your marksmanship). In my last vampire campaign, admittedly, the players who had celerity tended to forget they had that possibility, so my NPCs didn't abuse it, but provided combats aren't simple affair of rock'em sock'em robots, it can create a lot of opportunities (making someone drop a grenade before they can throw it for example) even outside of combat, it means you can stop someone from pressing a button or push someone who's going to get hurt away or something. The interruption thing is interesting because it can be used in many many ways. Then, there's the initiative boost, which is nice to have, but not crazy, and there's the speed boost which can make you extremely fast at high levels, like catching a car or, like the book says, passing through someone's field of view unnnoticed. It's pretty funny to think it took so many years for celerity to finally become both good and balanced.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Making celerity boost Dex would only make firearms the best choice period. Get a big enough gun, preferably with auto-fire and kill everything. Guns are already pretty underrated, probably due to the memory of 1E. One of my very average fighter players, towards the end of the campaign, finally decided, after I told her it was actually pretty good, to get and use a submachine gun and she was pretty damn effective with it, killing small groups of mooks in two turns basically, and making her pretty useful in the final boss fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T08:42:14-08:00","id":1006208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me#post1005544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mostly that it doesn't even really fit with the other two Physicals - plus, the extra resource you have to track offends my sense of aesthetics. Unt so:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>C</b>elerity</span><br /> <i>Insert descriptive text from B&amp;S here</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> None or One Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> None (For persistent effects) or Reflexive (For active effects)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent (For persistent effects) or Instant (For active effects)<br /> <br /> Like other physical Disciplines, Celerity has two kinds of effects: persistent and active. Persistent effects are always on, and have no cost. Active effects are Reflexive, and cost one Vitae per effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent:</b> Add the Vampire's dots in Celerity to their Dexterity; this may raise a character's Dexterity above the limit imposed by their Blood Potency. Additionally, add the Vampire's dots in Celerity to their Speed.<br /> <br /> <b>Active:</b> By spending Vitae, the Kindred may bring the frightful swiftness of their Beast to the fore, striking their victims before they even realize it. For every Vitae spent, chose one effect from the following list. A vampire may spend additional Vitae to invoke multiple effects simultaneously, but no effect of Celerity may be used more than once per turn.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Add thrice your dots in Celerity to your Speed this turn.<br /> \u2022 Attacks made against you this turn take a penalty equal to your dots in Celerity.<br /> \u2022 Immediately take the Break Free or Take Cover moves without rolling. <hr /><br /> It's rather different from the canon Celerity, I know - it's a bit more focused on being inhumanly agile and fast rather than being superhumanly fast.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> From what I am reading over here is that we have someone wanting to make Celerity better?<br /> <br /> Looking at the new mock up of the discipline. It is far weaker than Celerity as written. It doesn't make you faster, it actually makes you slower.<br /> <br /> Sure you can attack twice per round for a vitae, however as written you can interrupt their action. so STOPPING them from attacking you is better than you hitting them twice. You wait for them to take their attack and simply move, then attack them. Move and attack.. move and attack. That is better than Attack attack- get hit... attack attack, get hit. if you're not getting hit at all you can pretty much take up to 5 turns with them not being able to do anything ( especially if you call shot head, stun them on all of your turns. )<br /> <br /> using celerity to GO FIRST, beats getting +dots to your roll. you could roll a 1 and still go last.<br /> <br /> Having a higher dex doesnt actually let you be faster in the defense sense either, because you use the LOWER of your wits and dex to determine your init. Currently as written in the persistant side, celerity gives you the defense up to your dots, implying that you are faster. It allows you to apply defense to fire arms when normally you can not. Implying they are faster than a bullet, your write up does not allow for that. Yours you have to spend a vitae for that... you also have to know it's coming to spend vitae for it... RAW it's even if you dont know...<br /> <br /> Adding 3 to your speed is not better than multiplying your speed by your dots+ 1 for the turn. Say my speed is 10. Your power I can have 13 speed for a vitae. RAW: (celerity 1) I can have 20. Celerity 3 I can have 40. You have limited it to +3. Imagine if you will celerity 5 X speed 10 = my speed is 60 for a turn. That is infinitely better than 13<br /> <br /> In my opinion, you have made your vampire slower and weaker with this version of Celerity. <br /> <br /> <br /> with Celerity as written, verses your Celerity. Even if you could attack twice, the vampire with RAW celerity will just interrupt your turn and you will miss anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T09:34:58-08:00","id":1006233,"title":"","content":"I don't know about interruption being used to make people miss so easily. It's up to the GM I guess, but I wouldn't say using your interrupt action to move out of the way would automatically make the opponent miss. The opponent can move too. If you take the power as a miss if you blink interruption, then yes, it would work, but I don't think it's a very interesting or creative. I would allow moving out of the way if the character uses another vitae point to boost their speed so they move too far for the opponent to reach them and attack them for their action.<br /> <br /> When the book says that if the character does something that makes the opponent's action impossible, then the opponent loses their turn, I'm more thinking along the lines of grappling (preventing movement, or at least quick movement), disarming, grabbing an object before the opponent, that kind of thing. The hit and run tactic as permitted with that interpretation of celerity doesn't make for a very interesting or dramatic fight. Ok, actually, I would allow it, but only as long as the opponent doesn't understand what's going on.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm having another thought, now though, trying to picture the fight mechanically. So there's A and B. B has celerity. Maybe it's not that easy to do unless you're facing a wild boar.<br /> <br /> Round 1 :<br /> A and B are in melee range and are using brawl/weaponry.<br /> A attacks B<br /> B interrupts, hits and moves away.<br /> <br /> Round 2 :<br /> A and B are not in melee range.<br /> <br /> What now ?<br /> A can move towards B and attack.<br /> B will interrupt to replicate round 1. What happens then ? For it to work, that means B has to interrupt A between the move action and the attack action. Thematically, there's no problem with that, but mechanically, that means B isn't interrupting A's turn before it happens but in the middle of it happening. If B can only interrupt B's entire turn, then they have to get close before attacking, which will put them in A's range. Unless you consider that B moves basically behind A, attacks, and then B runs past A and attacks the spot B occupied at the start of round 2, putting them again out of melee range.<br /> <br /> Or else :<br /> A wises up and doesn't pursue, and instead waits for B to move towards them and attack so they can strike back. B can't get in, attack AND and get out in the same action. If B wants to attack, they must get in A's range and stay there. The interruption doesn't really help much there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T09:39:38-08:00","id":1006236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006233#post1006233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that means B isn't interrupting A's turn before it happens but in the middle of it happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>You <i>can't</i> interrupt something before it happens. You have to do it in the middle of it happening because <i>that's what interrupting means.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T10:03:33-08:00","id":1006252,"title":"","content":"Well, no, if you're interrupting someone while they're in the middle of stabbing you, you're not interrupting anything.<br /> <br /> My question is, do you choose the moment when you're going to interrupt the action, or do you have to do it at the start ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T10:10:53-08:00","id":1006255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006233#post1006233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about interruption being used to make people miss so easily. It's up to the GM I guess, but I wouldn't say using your interrupt action to move out of the way would automatically make the opponent miss. The opponent can move too. If you take the power as a miss if you blink interruption, then yes, it would work, but I don't think it's a very interesting or creative. I would allow moving out of the way if the character uses another vitae point to boost their speed so they move too far for the opponent to reach them and attack them for their action.<br /> <br /> When the book says that if the character does something that makes the opponent's action impossible, then the opponent loses their turn, I'm more thinking along the lines of grappling (preventing movement, or at least quick movement), disarming, grabbing an object before the opponent, that kind of thing. The hit and run tactic as permitted with that interpretation of celerity doesn't make for a very interesting or dramatic fight. Ok, actually, I would allow it, but only as long as the opponent doesn't understand what's going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>A: You take aim at your target who is 10 feet away, on your right side, you pull the Trigger. <br /> B: uses celerity to INTERRUPT that action by moving behind A. Since you are no longer where A aimed and fired at.. How can you possibly move. As celerity says you move too fast to see. You have to miss... though if you want A to Use Celerity to be able to change the action and interrupt the interrupt, you need a clash of wills to see who actually succeeded in the action. <br /> <br /> A: Swings his sword at the target right in front of him.<br /> B uses celerity to hop backward out of the range of the sword. How can the person hit if you are not even there. You already took the swing. <br /> <br /> <br /> And Elfive is correct. You are not interrupting before.. You are doing it in the middle. Like if someone is speaking and midway through the sentence you put your hand on their mouth to stop them. Their turn was speaking, your interruption was putting your hand on their mouth, preventing them from speaking, or rather being heard. <br /> <br /> You can only interrupt as many times as you have celerity dots..<br /> <br /> I do not mean to be rude, but I feel that perhaps the way Celerity works now is not fully understood. I am a firm believer in making sure you understand how it works RAW before you change it. so many many many people come to this site wanting to change how something works because they do not like it...but what happens (guessing) 90% of the time is that they did not know how it worked to begin with so their changes are often weaker than the original.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T10:19:16-08:00","id":1006260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006252#post1006252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, if you're interrupting someone while they're in the middle of stabbing you, you're not interrupting anything.<br /> <br /> My question is, do you choose the moment when you're going to interrupt the action, or do you have to do it at the start ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are interrupting the stabbing.. The very definition of interrupt is to stop someone from continuing the action they are taking.<br /> <br /> Correct me if I am wrong but the way chronicles works is that you call your actions on your turn, then roll dice<br /> <br /> A: I am going to swing at B<br /> B; when He attacks me I am going to move out of it with Celerity and shoot A<br /> C; I attack Bs new location<br /> <br /> B moves and Shoots, A misses. C either shoots or has to move and swing at B","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T12:15:50-08:00","id":1006325,"title":"","content":"You activate the Interrupt after someone announces their action. After you complete your Interrupt, they have to continue with the action they announced. If their action is no longer valid, it fails. So yes, if you Interrupt to move out of melee range after they declare a melee attack, they cannot change their mind and move before their attack. They already declared the attack. The attack fails because you are now out of range.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I'd allow that to block Ranged attacks unless you move out of line of sight. Or you could move behind cover to give them a penalty. But as long as you're still within range, I'd still let them roll it after being interrupted if it's ranged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:35:07-08:00","id":1006373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006260#post1006260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You are interrupting the stabbing.. The very definition of interrupt is to stop someone from continuing the action they are taking.<br /> <br /> Correct me if I am wrong but the way chronicles works is that you call your actions on your turn, then roll dice<br /> <br /> A: I am going to swing at B<br /> B; when He attacks me I am going to move out of it with Celerity and shoot A<br /> C; I attack Bs new location<br /> <br /> B moves and Shoots, A misses. C either shoots or has to move and swing at B</div> </div> </div> </div>No. B's action was to interrupt A. He doesn't get to interrupt AND attack in the same turn. That his action for the turn, C can still attack B, who gets the -1 to his Defense from being subjected to multiple attacks in the same turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:47:54-08:00","id":1006380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006373#post1006373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. B's action was to interrupt A. He doesn't get to interrupt AND attack in the same turn. That his action for the turn</div> </div> </div> </div>Attack is the very first example of what you can do after having interrupted another character. The interrupt is not an instant action. The interrupt allows you to take your instant action immediately before another declared action takes place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-21-2016, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T14:19:31-08:00","id":1006391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006380#post1006380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Attack is the very first example of what you can do after having interrupted another character. The interrupt is not an instant action. The interrupt allows you to take your instant action immediately before another declared action takes place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but you don't get two plus attacks or an enhanced movement radius and an attack in the same turn, which is what the scenario described. If you opt to use an attack method as your interrupt, you're effectively cutting just ahead of that person in initiative, that's it. You don't get to attack the person as part of an interrupt, then move to some out of range position so that your attacker can't reach you and proceed to make a ranged attack again in that same turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 11-21-2016, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T14:25:46-08:00","id":1006394,"title":"","content":"I think you're reading it wrong. B made one attack and then moved. C made the ranged attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T15:34:09-08:00","id":1006434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005654#post1005654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda think the Passive Power of Celerity isn't up to snuff.<br /> <br /> Vigor/Resilience get Strength/Stamina increases.<br /> Celerity gets Defense instead of Dexterity. I'm kinda fine with this, because giving Dex might not improve Defense, and Celerity is only about the speed part of Dexterity anyway.<br /> <br /> However Vigor also get extra attack dice in Melee, through the Strength. And jumping ability.<br /> Resilience get an extra health level. And the ability to downgrade non-sun aggravated damage.<br /> Celerity gets nothing else.<br /> <br /> The passive parts just don't seem very balanced.<br /> <br /> Passively I think they should still be faster. And not just in Defense. But in Attack too. Giving them Celerity bonus to their initiative would seem right to me. A 1 initiative per Celerity level (maybe even 2, or C+1). How do I answer a Daeva who says &quot;if I'm faster why don't I attack faster?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm honestly tempted to house rule it. And would but for the fact that I have literally, and deliberately, avoided doing any house rules.<br /> <br /> I wonder why the design choice was made to give them the short end of passive powers? Assuming they'd even accept they may have.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'd contend that Celerity does not have the short end of the passive powers, adding Celerity dots to Initiative IS something I wish I'd included. It's not remotely game breaking, and an entirely reasonable house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T15:37:12-08:00","id":1006436,"title":"","content":"No, B used Celerity to make a dodge action (instant action) as an interrupt and made a ranged attack (instant), or took a full move action (also an instant action) to move beyond the movement range of the attacker and make a ranged attack. That's not permissible under the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T15:47:45-08:00","id":1006440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006436#post1006436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, B used Celerity to make a dodge action (instant action)</div> </div> </div> </div>No they didn't? Nowhere in the example in question is Dodge mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006436#post1006436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or took a full move action (also an instant action) to move beyond the movement range of the attacker</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they didn't do that either. They used their regular movement to move beyond melee range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T17:39:56-08:00","id":1006479,"title":"","content":"The reason that active powers matter when talking about passive powers is the same reason that complaining the garnish on your 5 star steak meal is less amazing than someone else's italian hogie is unlikely to garner sympathy.<br /> <br /> You don't purchase the powers seperately. You purchase all of them at once for the same opportunity cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T17:42:33-08:00","id":1006481,"title":"","content":"Celerity 1 is, hands down, the most powerful physical discipline at one dot. Just opening up the ability to instant stealth move, the ability to surprise attack at will, the ability to autododge (Ideally followed by a gtfo), and the ability to go first when you *really* need to is worth the discipline's weight in gold.<br /> <br /> The defense bonus is... sure, its there. Its nice enough. Its not why you buy the discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T00:37:40-08:00","id":1006619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006440#post1006440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they didn't? Nowhere in the example in question is Dodge mentioned.<br /> <br /> No, they didn't do that either. They used their regular movement to move beyond melee range.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think tsusasi is particularly interested in what was actually written at this point. Admitting to be wrong can be a hard choice made harder by holding on to their mistake.<br /> <br /> Edit: I can clarify that moving out of range from an attack using the interrupt power of Celerity does not require any Dodge action. A Dodge is something you perform as an attack is happening. When you interrupt you allow yourself to act before the attack is happening. The attack doesn't happen until after you've taken your own action.<br /> <br /> Edit: I apologize, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a>. I should not have written that way about you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-23-2016, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T05:18:21-08:00","id":1006656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006619#post1006619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think tsusasi is particularly interested in what was actually written at this point. Admitting to be wrong can be a hard choice made harder by holding on to their mistake.<br /> <br /> Edit: I can clarify that moving out of range from an attack using the interrupt power of Celerity does not require any Dodge action. A Dodge is something you perform as an attack is happening. When you interrupt you allow yourself to act before the attack is happening. The attack doesn't happen until after you've taken your own action.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And the key point here is that the declared action must proceed as declared. So if I say &quot;I punch him in the face&quot; and then you follow with &quot;I interrupt, I move away from you&quot;, then I still have to punch.. the air sadly, as you're no longer there. Which you can then follow (during your normal turn) with &quot;shooting me in the face with the gun you had&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T06:35:36-08:00","id":1006679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006380#post1006380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Attack is the very first example of what you can do after having interrupted another character. The interrupt is not an instant action. The interrupt allows you to take your instant action immediately before another declared action takes place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think this is why we have so many people coming here to change the way things work. I am not sure if it is how it is written or if people do not read how it actually works. There is a disconnect between comprehension and the RAW. <br /> <br /> I will admit that even I question my interpretations of things, but in certain cases the RAW is extremely clear. You absolutely can interrupt and attack in the same turn. Interrupting is probably the equivalent of a reflexive action and you are still allowed an instant after that. Moving is not an instant action unless you spend your whole turn doing it, but you are allowed to move in a logical way a few feet to avoid or interrupt something. You couldn't attack and stun them to stop their turn and then attack them again. That would be 2 attacks, which is NOT what was said. Dodge move is also quite different than simply moving with celerity.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> - Thank you for clarifying for me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> much appreciated. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1157\" data-vbnamecard=\"1157\">SoulGambit</a> I 110% agree that celerity as a dot 1 power is more powerful than all the rest. Though if you dont know how to use it, it could seem incredibly weak. A sword is probably a deadly weapon and extremely dangerous... in my hands it would be a joke because I don't know how to use one...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T07:01:44-08:00","id":1006689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006679#post1006679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interrupting is probably the equivalent of a reflexive action</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not only the equivalent of a Reflexive Action, it literally is a Reflexive Action. All active effects are activated as Reflexive Actions, but I can understand if people miss that (especially when using the PDF) since that piece of information is on the page before the list of active effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T08:13:28-08:00","id":1006714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006689#post1006689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not only the equivalent of a Reflexive Action, it literally is a Reflexive Action. All active effects are activated as Reflexive Actions, but I can understand if people miss that (especially when using the PDF) since that piece of information is on the page before the list of active effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol! See. I did miss that ( or forgot ) I am just as guilty as the rest! <br /> (pst! I was looking at the PDF... )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T11:07:22-08:00","id":1006777,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a reflexive action that allows you to take an action that would otherwise be instant and/or use your movement, but prevents you from using a second instant action or moving more than your normal speed on your turn is a little unintuitive, I'm not surprised it's often misinterpreted.<br /> <br /> I wonder how many people missed that that's also how Dodging works in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T11:38:36-08:00","id":1006790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006777#post1006777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how many people missed that that's also how Dodging works in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Wait a second, what do you mean here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T11:46:00-08:00","id":1006792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006790#post1006790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Wait a second, what do you mean here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dodging is done Reflexively and uses up your Instant action for your turn. Check out CofD page 88 (or Requiem page 176):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At any point before a character\u2019s action, she can choose to Dodge. Doing so takes up her normal action. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-22-2016, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T11:52:02-08:00","id":1006794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006792#post1006792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dodging is done Reflexively and uses up your Instant action for your turn. Check out CofD page 88 (of Requiem page 176):</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh phew! For a second I thought I had dodge all messed up. And thanks for the effort of the page references.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T15:38:55-08:00","id":1006886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1005720#post1005720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why you're saying &quot;except towards a hostile party.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that is what is implied with the Defense bonus - Moving faster and having better reaction speed to avoid incoming attacks. So fast in fact, that firearms are penalized as well, but you can only move that fast to avoid things and not towards an enemy. I do understand about the action economy, though when it is a choice between attack or move, then it is really only firearms which would get a big boost in contrast to Vigor which has just as powerful an effect on melee attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006679#post1006679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is why we have so many people coming here to change the way things work. I am not sure if it is how it is written or if people do not read how it actually works. There is a disconnect between comprehension and the RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it is poorly worded.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T18:07:51-08:00","id":1006940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006619#post1006619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think tsusasi is particularly interested in what was actually written at this point. Admitting to be wrong can be a hard choice made harder by holding on to their mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You can leave the editorializing about other users out of your replies, it's a rule 1 violation. Please do not do so again.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T10:24:09-08:00","id":1007309,"title":"","content":"The discipline could be better worded. Honestly, sometimes, a drawing is easier to understand than a sentence compressed to explain everything in as few words as possible.<br /> <br /> &quot; Interrupt the action of another character with a brief action of her own. This could be an attack, making it possible to disable an opponent in mid-action. It may be movement, avoiding harm by shifting out of reach. Or it could be any other instant action, like activating a Discipline or dodging.&quot;<br /> <br /> The text says that moving out of the way of an attack means moving &quot;out of reach&quot;, so getting behind someone who's about to shoot you is up to interpretation (although moving in melee range as they're about to shoot you would at least let you use your defence).<br /> <br /> But wait a minute, there's something weird about that, compared to what Charlaquin just posted about dodging :<br /> <br /> &quot;At any point before a character's action, she can choose to Dodge. Doing so takes up her normal action.&quot;<br /> <br /> If someone can declare they dodge at any point before they get to act, how does Celerity help ?<br /> <br /> <br /> But that's a minor point. I'm more interested by the part about moving. Normally, you can move up to your speed and take an instant action as well. The wording of the interruption power of celerity seems to suggest that you can't both move and take action. Does that mean that you have to choose for your whole turn or that you can do the other part of your action at your normal turn ?<br /> <br /> Like :<br /> A has initiative 9, B has initiative 5<br /> At 9 : A melee attacks B. B interrupts and moves out of reach but cannot do that AND attack.<br /> At 5 : B is out of reach and shoots A ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T11:15:29-08:00","id":1007335,"title":"","content":"You can take one instant action and move up to your speed in a given round. Celerity has no effect on this, aside from potentially making &quot;your speed&quot; a much larger number. <br /> <br /> What Celerity does is effectively let you take part or all of your turn <i>during</i> another character's. When it gets to where your turn <i>should</i> have gone, you can take the rest of it, if there's anything left you haven't already spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T13:14:02-08:00","id":1007394,"title":"","content":"So then you can both (for example) move and attack as your interruption. Because the way the discipline is written can be understood as saying you can't do both (and have to choose one to do now, and the other at your normal turn) : &quot;a brief action&quot;, and presenting the movement separately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1007335#post1007335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">let you take part or all of your turn</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the rest, this is the point I'm interested in.<br /> <br /> I don't want to be a bother, but while the core idea of &quot;you can act just as another character is about to act or acting&quot; is clear enough, that specific bit about splitting your action and movement being just an option or mandatory is a subtlety the description doesn't really make very clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T14:57:05-08:00","id":1007446,"title":"","content":"If it ain't clear, just go with what feels right. That's how I do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T10:53:07-08:00","id":1008974,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I don't particularly think that celerity is poorly written. While I do think several things are left vague so that story tellers and players interpret things differently, Celerity is one of the more clear things in the game. It is completely straightforward and has a list of examples on how to use it. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1007309#post1007309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The discipline could be better worded. Honestly, sometimes, a drawing is easier to understand than a sentence compressed to explain everything in as few words as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1007309#post1007309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot; Interrupt the action of another character with a brief action of her own. This could be an attack, making it possible to disable an opponent in mid-action. It may be movement, avoiding harm by shifting out of reach. Or it could be any other instant action, like activating a Discipline or dodging.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The text says that moving out of the way of an attack means moving &quot;out of reach&quot;, so getting behind someone who's about to shoot you is up to interpretation (although moving in melee range as they're about to shoot you would at least let you use your defence).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You are allowed to interrupt your opponent's turn by spending a vitae. here are a few examples. Attacking, moving, dodging, disciplines, or other instant actions. How you use those options is entirely up to you. We(here) have given you examples as well. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Moving: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You move out of their reach, you move behind them, you move behind a wall, you close the door. You initiate a grapple, means they lose their called action and now have to deal with that. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Disciplines: You kick off Idol, or Nightmare them away, or burst into a swarm. who knows. that's your call. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Attacking: pretty self explanatory You interrupt by swinging first and hand wrack them, they can no longer take their action of shooting you. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1007309#post1007309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But wait a minute, there's something weird about that, compared to what Charlaquin just posted about dodging :</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1007309#post1007309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;At any point before a character's action, she can choose to Dodge. Doing so takes up her normal action.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If someone can declare they dodge at any point before they get to act, how does Celerity help ?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As far as why dodging might be chosen, is again up to you. Maybe you are in a small confined room and there is no where else to go. Maybe you dont have a lot of vitae to spend on doing other disciplines too, maybe you're just playing keep away. It's situational and not required. Simply moving out of the way and dodging are two different actions, while playing you will choose which one is more appropriate for your character. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1007309#post1007309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But that's a minor point. I'm more interested by the part about moving. Normally, you can move up to your speed and take an instant action as well. The wording of the interruption power of celerity seems to suggest that you can't both move and take action. Does that mean that you have to choose for your whole turn or that you can do the other part of your action at your normal turn ?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Like :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A has initiative 9, B has initiative 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">At 9 : A melee attacks B. B interrupts and moves out of reach but cannot do that AND attack.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">At 5 : B is out of reach and shoots A ?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It does not imply that you can't do both. It very clearly says you cant take 2 instant actions, which would be something like 2 attacks.<i> (&quot;</i></span></span></span><i>the vampire is still limited to one instant action&quot; ) </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> It says nothing about not being able to move and attack. I believe it says that you can interrupt with an attack to clarify that is something that you CAN do. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There has already been an example of how to do this. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1006260#post1006260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A: I am going to swing at B<br /> B; when He attacks me I am going to move out of it with Celerity and shoot A<br /> C; I attack Bs new location<br /> <br /> B moves and Shoots, A misses. C either shoots or has to move and swing at B</div> </div> </div> </div>No dodging, the interrupt was moving with Celerity. Using Celerity does not cancel out my turn since it is a REFLEXIVE action. So I still get a turn to attack which is an instant action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T11:10:58-08:00","id":1008980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1005544-discipline-celerity-bugs-me?p=1008974#post1008974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As far as why dodging might be chosen, is again up to you. Maybe you are in a small confined room and there is no where else to go. Maybe you dont have a lot of vitae to spend on doing other disciplines too, maybe you're just playing keep away. It's situational and not required. Simply moving out of the way and dodging are two different actions, while playing you will choose which one is more appropriate for your character. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The reason Dodging specifically is a weird example is that you can already Dodge at any time before your action, just by the normal Dodging rules. So it would be kind of silly to spend a Vitae and one of your limited number of uses per scene of Celerity's interrupt ability to Dodge as a Reflexive action, since you can already Dodge as a Reflexive action without doing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T12:11:07-08:00","id":1008997,"title":"","content":"It says you can dodge, not Dodge. I think it just means &quot;move out of the way&quot; there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}